{"base_rate":0.4953764861294584,"brier":0.22942774108322322,"bss":0.08221055776614317,"bss_hi":0.18847831554021036,"bss_lo":-0.023290818849337307,"chart":{"base":[704.3,207.1],"fp":[454.8,232.1],"lead":"62,133.8 272,130 482,124.4 692,107.3","note":{"base":"skill 0.08 — higher than 10% of cities","fp":"low end +21pp, high end +20pp","lead":"day-1 error 2.2 °C — better than 1% of cities","rel":"promised 3% → rained 25%; promised 94% → rained 74%"},"rel":"83.1,359.1 333.9,254.2 656.4,145.2"},"country":"GB","deep":false,"depth":["Rain-probability calibration","Calibration curve","Seasonal split"],"ece":0.1769881109643329,"ess":401.52453485009113,"html":{"answer":"\n<h2 id=\"answer\">The short answer for Nottingham</h2>\n<div class=\"verdict\">\n<p class=\"lead\"><b>The Nottingham rain forecast is only marginally better than quoting the long-run average, though 5 points on its probability scale are off by more than chance explains.</b></p>\n<p>When it says rain is <i>near certain</i> (99%), believe about\n<b>78%</b>. When it says rain is <i>very unlikely</i>\n(1%), there is still roughly a <b>19%</b> chance.</p>\n<p class=\"muted\">Based on 757 days, 2024-04-26 to\n2026-05-31. \"Rain\" means at least 0.2 mm measured at\nNOTTINGHAM: WATNALL, 8.8 km from the forecast grid point.\nSkill score 0.08, ranked 120 of\n134 &mdash; but see the rank <i>range</i>\n(107&ndash;128) before reading anything into\nthat position.</p>\n</div>\n\n<h3>What the percentages actually mean here</h3>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th class=\"num\">It said</th><th class=\"num\">It rained</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Days</th><th>Verdict</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td class='num'>1%</td><td class='num'><b>19%</b></td><td class='num'>222</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">underpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>11%</td><td class='num'><b>42%</b></td><td class='num'>77</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">underpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>30%</td><td class='num'><b>41%</b></td><td class='num'>76</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">underpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>56%</td><td class='num'><b>57%</b></td><td class='num'>79</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>82%</td><td class='num'><b>62%</b></td><td class='num'>76</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>99%</td><td class='num'><b>78%</b></td><td class='num'>227</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">5 of 6 groups are further from honest than chance\nalone can explain. The rest are indistinguishable from a perfect forecast.</p>\n","card":"\n<div class=\"gcard\">\n  <p class=\"gcard-head\"><b>Nottingham</b> <span class=\"muted\">GB</span></p>\n  <p class=\"gcard-tier\"><span class=\"tag bad\">Barely beats the average</span>\n    <span class=\"muted\">5 points off by more than chance</span></p>\n  <dl class=\"gcard-stats\">\n    <div><dt>Skill score</dt><dd>0.08</dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Rank</dt><dd>107&ndash;128\n      <span class=\"muted\">of 134</span></dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Record</dt><dd>757 <span class=\"muted\">days</span></dd></div>\n  </dl>\n  <p class=\"gcard-more\"><a href=\"#answer\">The full verdict for\n    Nottingham &darr;</a></p>\n</div>","curve":"\n<h2 id=\"curve\">The calibration curve</h2>\n<p>Each dot is a group of days sharing a similar forecast. Horizontal position\nis what was promised; vertical is what happened. <b>On the dashed diagonal =\nhonest.</b> Hover any dot for its sample size.</p>\n<figure><svg viewBox=\"0 0 430 430\" width=\"100%\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Calibration curve for Nottingham\"><rect class=\"chart-plot\" x=\"58\" y=\"18\" width=\"354\" height=\"364\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"58\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"382\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"58\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">0%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"386\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">0%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"146.5\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"146.5\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"291.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"291.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"146.5\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">25%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"295.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">25%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"235.0\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"235.0\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"200.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"200.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"235.0\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">50%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"204.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">50%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"323.5\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"323.5\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"109.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"109.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"323.5\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">75%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"113.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">75%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"412\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"18\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"412\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">100%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"22\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">100%</text><polygon class=\"chart-band\" points=\"60.36,375.44144144144144 97.26181818181819,315.8181818181818 164.20000000000002,238.31578947368422 255.6126582278481,137.79746835443038 346.5565789473684,56.31578947368422 407.24361233480175,18.0 407.24361233480175,27.621145374449327 346.5565789473684,118.57894736842104 255.6126582278481,216.24177215189874 164.20000000000002,310.1578947368421 97.26181818181819,363.09090909090907 60.36,382.0\" opacity=\"0.16\"/><line class=\"chart-ideal\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\" stroke-dasharray=\"5,4\" stroke-width=\"1.3\"/><line class=\"chart-base\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"201.68295904887714\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"201.68295904887714\" stroke-dasharray=\"2,3\"/><polyline class=\"chart-line\" points=\"60.36,313.1351351351351 97.26181818181819,230.72727272727272 164.20000000000002,233.5263157894737 255.6126582278481,174.65822784810126 346.5565789473684,156.89473684210526 407.24361233480175,96.57268722466961\" fill=\"none\" stroke-width=\"2.4\"/><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 1%&amp;#10;It rained 19% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 222 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"60.36\" cy=\"313.1351351351351\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 11%&amp;#10;It rained 42% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 77 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"97.26181818181819\" cy=\"230.72727272727272\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 30%&amp;#10;It rained 41% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 76 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"164.20000000000002\" cy=\"233.5263157894737\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 56%&amp;#10;It rained 57% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 79 days&amp;#10;within the range a perfect forecast would give\"><circle class=\"chart-dot\" cx=\"255.6126582278481\" cy=\"174.65822784810126\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 82%&amp;#10;It rained 62% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 76 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"346.5565789473684\" cy=\"156.89473684210526\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 99%&amp;#10;It rained 78% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 227 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"407.24361233480175\" cy=\"96.57268722466961\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"235.0\" y=\"422\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\">What the forecast promised</text><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"15\" y=\"200.0\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\" transform=\"rotate(-90 15 200.0)\">How often it actually rained</text></svg>\n<figcaption>Green band = where a <b>flawless</b> forecast would still land, given\nhow few days we have. Red dots fall outside it, so those are real errors rather\nthan noise. The faint horizontal line is climatology\n(50%).</figcaption></figure>\n","season":"\n<h2 id=\"season\">Does the season matter?</h2>\n<p>In Nottingham the forecast is most skilful in\n<b>spring</b> (0.15) and least in\n<b>winter</b> (-0.34).</p>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th>Season</th><th class=\"num\">Days</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Rain days</th><th class=\"num\">Skill score</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Avg error</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>winter</td><td class='num'>175</td><td class='num'>71%</td><td class='num'>-0.339</td><td class='num'>25.1%</td></tr><tr><td>summer</td><td class='num'>184</td><td class='num'>36%</td><td class='num'>-0.049</td><td class='num'>19.3%</td></tr><tr><td>autumn</td><td class='num'>180</td><td class='num'>62%</td><td class='num'>0.078</td><td class='num'>16.7%</td></tr><tr><td>spring</td><td class='num'>218</td><td class='num'>34%</td><td class='num'>0.148</td><td class='num'>11.9%</td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">Four-way splits of a two-year record are thin, so read the\nordering as indicative. Coarser binning is used here than for the annual curve\nfor the same reason.</p>\n"},"lat":52.9536,"lon":-1.15047,"n":757,"n_cities":134,"name":"Nottingham","offset_days":1,"pop_map":[{"hi":0.06,"lo":0.0,"mean":0.006666666666666666,"n":222,"obs":0.1891891891891892,"sig":true},{"hi":0.2,"lo":0.06,"mean